      "text_en": "Residual Anomaly: RA-047 · Decoy Interference\nAssigned Will: Layer XII · Engine Prime\nAnomalous Overview: In pre-containment state, the anomaly could insert fabricated passages into any codex, maintaining grammatical consistency while inverting semantic meaning. Affected texts induced cognitive reversal upon completion of reading, including the documented mass aphasia incident in Scriptorium ██. Identification of forged content requires word-by-word comparison with original codices, though the comparison process itself triggers secondary effects.\nContainment Residue: Under Engine suppression, the anomaly can only generate visually similar but meaningless pseudo-glyphs during inscription. Keybound report 'some slugs look correct but make no sound when struck.'\nAddendum: F-017 incident reports indicate keybound who perfectly identify all decoy glyphs disappear within the day. Per §4.2(b), such performance is now classified as 'excessive competency' requiring immediate reassignment.\n——'Truth mingles with false words; only the humble discern the true glyph's form'"
